2. Mathematical Preliminaries and State‑Space Formulation

Before defining the system, we establish a common mathematical framework that will be used throughout the thesis.

2.1 State‑Space and Design Parameter Space

The MHAS is a rigid body with a time‑varying mass distribution. Its instantaneous state is defined on a 14-dimensional manifold \mathcal{S} \subset \mathbb{R}^{14}:

\mathbf{x}(t) = \big[ \mathbf{p}(t),\; \mathbf{v}(t),\; \mathbf{q}(t),\; \boldsymbol{\omega}(t),\; m_{\text{total}}(t),\; E_{\text{stored}}(t) \big]^\top

where \mathbf{p}\in\mathbb{R}^3 is position, \mathbf{v} velocity, \mathbf{q} a unit quaternion representing attitude, \boldsymbol{\omega} angular velocity in the body frame, m_{\text{total}} total system mass (including propellant), and E_{\text{stored}} the remaining usable energy.

The design parameter vector captures the mass allocation and component choices:

\boldsymbol{\theta} = [m_{\text{struct}}, m_E, m_{\text{prop}}, \mathbf{\tau}_{\max}, \text{material choice}, \dots]^\top \in \Theta \subset \mathbb{R}^p.

All constraints (thrust, torque, strength, energy density) are expressed as inequalities g_i(\boldsymbol{\theta}) \le 0, i=1,\dots,k.

2.2 Dynamical Equations

The translation is governed by Newton’s second law for a variable‑mass system:

m_{\text{total}}(t)\, \dot{\mathbf{v}} = \mathbf{F}_{\text{thrust}} + \mathbf{F}_{\text{aero}} + \mathbf{F}_{\text{contact}} - \dot m_{\text{total}}(t)\,\mathbf{v}_e + m_{\text{total}}(t)\,\mathbf{g}_p,

where \dot m_{\text{total}} \le 0 accounts for propellant ejection with exhaust velocity \mathbf{v}_e (for rocket‑based propulsion). The term \mathbf{F}_{\text{aero}} vanishes on the Moon.

The attitude dynamics use the Euler equation with time‑varying inertia tensor \mathbf{I}(t):

\mathbf{I}(t)\,\dot{\boldsymbol{\omega}} + \boldsymbol{\omega} \times \big(\mathbf{I}(t)\,\boldsymbol{\omega}\big) = \mathbf{M}_{\text{thrust}} + \mathbf{M}_{\text{exo}},

where \mathbf{M}_{\text{thrust}} is the control moment from differential throttling or gimbaling.

