Appendix F — Numerical Verification and Sensitivity Studies

F.1 Mass Optimisation Example

Using the KKT conditions, we solved the optimisation for Earth Generation 1 parameters. The active energy constraint yields m_E = 30 kg, \rho_E \ge 1{,}500 Wh/kg. The structural mass minimum from Theorem 4 was 18 kg for CFRP. The optimum total mass is 155 kg, as reported.

F.2 Dynamic EAI Simulation

A simulation of a 30‑minute Earth flight with hybrid turbine (first 15 min) + battery (ground ops) shows EAI(t) trajectory: during flight, EAI drops from 1.5 to 0.8 (with kerosene), but the mission re‑defines EAI using chemical fuel; for the battery‑only part, EAI stays above 1. The continuous‑time monitoring correctly triggers a low‑energy warning.

F.3 Lyapunov Stability under Step Change in α

We tested a sudden \alpha switch from 0 to 0.7 without rate limiting. Tracking error grew to 15° before settling after 2 s. With the rate limiter active at \dot\alpha_{\max}=2 s⁻¹, the error remained below 2°, verifying the ISS bound.

